      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T19:49:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e\u003eDoes that mean this patch isn\u0027t needed for now?\n\nWe are able to add sync awareness for rt in walt. With that we arent critically dependent on this patch (for now).\n\n\u003e\u003eYes, but even more generally, we prefer code that has been vetted upstream. If we are going to diverge from that, we prefer to isolate the divergent behavior into vendor code.\n\nshould_honor_rt_sync()  is not upstream AFAICT. This was a google addition perhaps requested by some OEM. I dont have access to BUG 157906395 which attempts to limit what rt tasks are migrateable\n\n\"\n ANDROID: sched/rt: Add support for rt sync wakeups\n\n    Some rt tasks undergo sync wakeup. Currently, these tasks will be placed\n    on other, often sleeping or otherwise idle CPUs, which can lead to\n    unnecessary power hits.\n\n    Bug: 157906395  \n \"\n\n\n\n\u003e\u003eWhat are you proposing?\n\n\nDrop the  task_has_rt_policy(rq-\u003ecurr)  in  should_honor_rt_sync()  we  should  honor a  rt sync even if a CFS task wakes up RT task.",
      "parentUuid": "577ac9dc_5fbbcc54",
      "revId": "b05f5d15f8598a81c1b2562a272633ca2b50174a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "146f6995_5513770f",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1411,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T20:03:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We are able to add sync awareness for rt in walt. With that we arent critically dependent on this patch (for now).\n\nCan we abandon this patch and close the bug then?\n\n\u003e should_honor_rt_sync()  is not upstream AFAICT.\n\nYes, you are right. This is a perf optimization for cases where 2 RT threads are communicating.\n\n\u003e Drop the  task_has_rt_policy(rq-\u003ecurr)  in  should_honor_rt_sync()  we  should  honor a  rt sync even if a CFS task wakes up RT task.\n\nCan you file a bug with your rationale for this? I think your claim is that immediately preempting the CFS waker doesn\u0027t actually result in an extra wake for the tail of the CFS task since the RT task will have provided more for the CFS task to do. To me, that sounds very workload dependent, but we can discuss in the bug.",
      "parentUuid": "6f110d57_2368b3ea",
      "revId": "b05f5d15f8598a81c1b2562a272633ca2b50174a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
